 "prof.h":"👤 My profile","prof.name":"Name (for the greeting in the header)","hello":"Hi, {name}!","prof.industry":"Industry","prof.tenure":"Tenure, years","prof.kids0":"Children under 6","prof.kids6":"Children 6–17","prof.extra":"Extra credit points","prof.hish":"I have keren hishtalmut (7.5% / 2.5%)",
 "brk.hish":"Keren hishtalmut (2.5%)","employer.hish":"Employer keren hishtalmut (7.5%)","ot.add":"➕ Add to gross in the calculator",
 "ai.t.morepoints":"<b>What earns tax credit points (נקודות זיכוי; each = −242 ₪ tax/month, 2,904 ₪/year):</b><br>• <b>Children</b> — counted automatically in the calculator («Children under 6» / «6–17»).<br>• <b>New immigrants</b> — automatic by aliyah date (54 privileged months).<br>• <b>Discharged soldiers:</b> full service — 2 points, partial — 1; for the first 36 months after discharge.<br>• <b>Academic degree:</b> BA — 1 point, MA — 0.5 (usually the year after graduation; professional diploma — 0.5).<br>• <b>Alimony</b> to an ex-spouse — +1.<br>• <b>Single parent</b> — extra points.<br>• <b>Non-working spouse</b> — 1 point if the spouse has no income and retirement age (or disability) applies.<br>• 100% disability / blindness — not points but an income-tax exemption (sec. 9(5)).<br>• Residents of peripheral towns — a 7–20% tax discount per the official list.<br><b>How to claim:</b> mark the grounds in Form 101 with your employer; missed past years — tax refund up to 6 years back. Whatever isn't automatic (soldier, degree, alimony…) — enter the total in the «Extra points» field and the net recalculates.",
 "prof.ind.general":"General","prof.ind.cleaning":"Cleaning","prof.ind.security":"Security","prof.ind.construction":"Construction","prof.ind.catering":"Catering","prof.ind.care":"Caregiving",
 "prof.hint":"Your profile is stored on the device and tunes the whole app. Child credit points are counted automatically: under 6 — 4.5 points to each parent, 6–17 — mother 2 / father 1. Important: points apply only to children living with you in Israel — no points for children who stayed abroad (birth year and the year of turning 18 give partial points). Don't forget to mark the children in Form 101!",
 "prof.hish.hint":"<b>What it is:</b> keren hishtalmut (קרן השתלמות) — your personal tax-advantaged savings fund, a «second pension».<br><b>How it fills up:</b> 2.5% from your salary + 7.5% added by the employer = 10% a month into your account.<br><b>When to withdraw:</b> after 6 years — the whole amount, tax-free.<br><b>Who must get it (extension orders):</b><br>• cleaning and security — from day one;<br>• construction — site workers after <b>3 years of seniority in the industry</b> (in Israel, across all employers); foremen and crane operators — from day 1. Office staff of construction firms (accounting, HR, marketing) are NOT covered by the construction order;<br>• <b>foreign construction workers (B1/2a5) don't get a fund opened</b> — instead, after 3 years of industry seniority they're owed a cash supplement «chalaf hishtalmut» (חלף השתלמות). No supplement — underpayment;<br>• manpower-agency workers may fall under a different agreement.<br>In other industries — only if your contract says so.<br><b>Simple rule:</b> the השתלמות line exists in your payslip → tick the box; no line → untick (and if the list above entitles you — demand it in writing).<br><b>Nuance:</b> percentages apply to the base salary — overtime and one-off bonuses aren't included (the app calculates it that way).",
 "fired.h":"Dismissal calculator: what am I owed","fired.hint":"A legal-minimum estimate for dismissal by the employer (or equivalent resignation). Fill in — see the full settlement.",
 "fired.paytype":"Pay type","fired.monthly":"Monthly","fired.hourlyp":"Hourly",
 "fired.gross":"Last gross, ₪/month","fired.tenure":"Tenure, years","fired.vacdays":"Unused vacation days","fired.havdays":"Unpaid havra'a days",
 "fired.res.pitz":"Pitzuim (פיצויי פיטורים) — severance pay","fired.res.notice":"Hodaa mukdemet (הודעה מוקדמת) — notice pay, days:","fired.res.vac":"Pidyon chufsha (פדיון חופשה) — unused vacation payout","fired.res.hav":"Dmey havraa (דמי הבראה) — recreation pay","fired.total":"Total settlement",
 "fired.note":"<b>How to read this estimate:</b><br>• <b>Pitzuim (פיצויי פיטורים — severance pay):</b> one monthly gross salary per year worked; due after a full year of tenure.<br>• <b>Check the «Section 14» clause (סעיף 14) in your contract.</b> Most contracts have it, and it means: the employer has already been depositing your severance monthly — 8.33% of salary — into your pension fund. In that case you collect that money FROM THE FUND (call them and ask for the severance component), not from the employer. If only 6% was deposited — the employer tops up the difference himself.<br>• <b>Pidyon chufsha (פדיון חופשה — payout of unused vacation):</b> a vacation day = gross ÷ 21.67 (5-day week).<br>• <b>Havraa (דמי הבראה — annual recreation pay, due after one year):</b> calculated at your sector's daily rate: cleaning/security/public — 511.60 ₪, private — 418 ₪.<br>• All of this is the legal minimum; sectors with a tzav harchava (צו הרחבה — an extension order applying a collective agreement to the whole sector) may owe you more.<br>• An employment-period certificate must be issued within 14 days of dismissal.<br>⚠️ <b>Court deadlines:</b> a claim for unpaid vacation — up to 3 years from dismissal; claims for unpaid wages and severance — up to 7 years.",
 "emp.ot.exp":"➕ This month's overtime (125% / 150%)","emp.ot.hint":"The hourly rate is taken automatically: gross ÷ 182. The overtime pay joins the taxable gross — income tax and National Insurance are computed on the full amount, while pension and hishtalmut, as the law requires, are computed on the base salary only.",
 "brk.ot":"Overtime (125/150%)","brk.taxbase":"Taxable gross (base + overtime)",
